        "text": "select the Tables icon.\n244   PART 3 Getting Things Done\nA query allows you to ask complex questions regarding your database.\nThe Tasks pane\nThe upper-right pane is the Tasks pane. In here, you see what types of things you\ncan do for a particular selection in the Database pane. Use the Description to the\nright to decrypt any of the terms that make your eyes cross.\nThe Tables/Queries/Forms/Reports pane\nThe lower-right pane shows the tables, queries, forms, or reports that already\nexist. You can open any of these to work in by double-clicking them in this pane.\nTABLE 12-7\nThe LibreOffice Base Standard Toolbar, from Left to Right\nButton or Item\nWhat You Can Do\nNew\nOpen new documents of various types. Click the downward arrow to select a\nparticular type of document to create, from among any of the OOo types.",
